    "description": "Néstor de Jesús Guishard, a school counselor in Río Piedras and doctoral student, was imprisoned following the May 2003 protests surrounding the U.S. Navy departure from Vieques. He was convicted of destruction of U.S. government property and initially sentenced to eight months. Six additional months were imposed when his probation was revoked. He was released from MDC Guaynabo on December 9, 2004."
